; na.claims — the property names `b.ghost`, an arrow the `box` type does not
; declare. Kernel §8: a property naming structure the schema lacks is n/a —
; reported, but never a pass and never exit 1. Before the fix, parse-time path
; type-checking of property formulas rejected the unknown arrow outright (a hard
; parse error → exit 2); now the shape is decoded and arrow resolution is
; deferred to the checker, which returns n/a → exit 0.

(property phantom-arrow "a property naming an arrow the schema lacks"
  (possible (is b.ghost hi)))
